        {
          "type": "risk",
          "priority": "medium",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T11:11:34Z",
          "note": "A05 Security Misconfiguration / A01 Broken Access Control — MEDIUM (pre-existing, non-blocking). api-knowledge.ts handleDeleteKnowledge (line 303) and handlePromoteKnowledge (line 371): repository_name query parameter is NOT validated against PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX at the handler layer. The storage layer's _validateSlug() prevents path traversal before any file path is constructed, so no security breach is possible. However, a malformed slug causes _validateSlug() to throw a generic Error (not an ApiError), which propagates to the unhandled-error branch and returns HTTP 500 instead of a well-typed HTTP 400 VALIDATION_ERROR. This is a documented known limitation in the file's @known-limitation comment. Contrast: handleMoveKnowledge and handleUpdateKnowledge both validate repository_name via Zod PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX before storage access. Recommended fix: add an explicit z.string().regex(PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX) guard to handleDeleteKnowledge and handlePromoteKnowledge to return consistent 400 responses and eliminate reliance on the storage layer as the sole validation point. This was NOT introduced by WP-008 — it pre-dates this work package."
