        {
          "type": "improvement",
          "priority": "low",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-30T11:11:34Z",
          "note": "A03 Injection (API layer) — PASS. api-client.js buildQueryString() uses encodeURIComponent() on all key/value pairs (line 45), preventing query-string injection. URL path segments (id, slug) are encoded via encodeURIComponent() at all call sites. Request bodies are serialised via JSON.stringify(), preventing injection through body parameters. moveKnowledge() passes targetRepositoryName directly to the JSON body without coercion — this is validated server-side by KnowledgeMoveBodySchema z.string().regex(PROJECT_SLUG_REGEX), providing proper server-side input validation."
        },
